  "question": {
    "text": "For the cell $\\mathrm{Zn}(\\mathrm{s})\\left|\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(\\mathrm{aq}) \\| \\mathrm{M}^{\\mathrm{x}+}(\\mathrm{aq})\\right| \\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{s}),$ different half\r\n\r\ncells and their standard electrode potentials are given below:\r\n\r\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0146_9fab5f132989.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nIf $\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+} / \\mathrm{Zn}}^{\\circ}=-0.76 \\mathrm{~V},$ which cathode will give a maximum value of $E_{\\text {cell }}^{0}$ per electron transferred?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Ag}^{+} / \\mathrm{Ag}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Fe}^{3+} / \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Au}^{3+} / \\mathrm{Au}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+} / \\mathrm{Fe}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{Zn}+2 \\mathrm{Ag}^{+} \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{Ag}+\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\\left(n=2 e^{-}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$=0.80-(-0.76)=1.56 \\mathrm{~V}$ for $2 e$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}$ for $1 e^{-}=\\frac{1.56}{2}=0.78 \\mathrm{~V}$"
  }
